The  framework  provides  support  to handle hardware monitor de‐
vices.  Hardware monitoring chips are able to report values  from
different types of sensors.  The framework consists of two parts:
the  userland part, to receive the current sensor data and to set
some properties on sensors: The kernel part that is able to  talk
to the devices providing sensor data: The framework uses for com‐
munication  between  kernel  and user space.  The following types
are available: This is used to receive the global dictionary that
is being used in the kernel by the framework.  It will contain an
array of dictionaries per device and one  dictionary  per  sensor
plus  another special dictionary that contains the properties for
a device.  Each sensor dictionary will have its own  characteris‐
tics  and  values.   The following XML property list represents a
virtual device with one entry for sensor and all available  prop‐
erties  set  on  it, plus another entry for the dictionary (which
